# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("`rebuild`": holds start over; places are new under the next `#g`; a generation is built at the end of the tick its dynamic changes; the old generation runs to the end of its tick, requests included, and its events become `never`) and ch. 8 ("The patch": a place built at the end of n is added in n, one that leaves at the end of n is removed in n).
test an_old_generation_is_silent

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="next")
    1: Ui.Button(label="ring")
    2/#0/0: Ui.Button(label="hit 1")
    2/#0/1: Test.Log
    2/#0/2: Ui.Label(text="page 1: 0 hits")

tick 1
  in:
    2/#0/0: click
  changed:
    2/#0/2: Ui.Label(text="page 1: 1 hits")

tick 2
  in:
    0: click
    1: click
  added:
    2/#1/0: Ui.Button(label="hit 2")
    2/#1/1: Test.Log
    2/#1/2: Ui.Label(text="page 2: 0 hits")
  torn down:
    2/#0/0: Ui.Button(label="hit 1")
    2/#0/1: Test.Log
    2/#0/2: Ui.Label(text="page 1: 1 hits")
  requested:
    2/#0/1: "ring 1"

tick 3
  in:
    1: click
  requested:
    2/#1/1: "ring 2"

tick 4
  in:
    2/#1/0: click
  changed:
    2/#1/2: Ui.Label(text="page 2: 1 hits")
